PAGE = dict(
    slug='align_xy',
    title='Pane::align_xy',
    signature='Pane& Pane::align_xy(std::string group)',
    intro='Puts both the x and the y axis of the pane into the alignment group `group`: the one call for panes whose rows and columns should line up.\n\nThe call is the same as [`align_x(group)`](align_x.md) and [`align_y(group)`](align_y.md): each axis joins the group `group`, and everything [`align_x`](align_x.md) says about a group (a shared range, hand-set limits winning, one shared caption) holds for each axis separately. The axes are independent groups that happen to carry the same name, so a caption for the x group and one for the y group are two captions, written by [`x_caption`](../studio/x_caption.md) and [`y_caption`](../studio/y_caption.md).\n\nUse it for panes that are copies of one another in layout (small multiples), where every axis should line up. When only one axis should line up, call the single-axis form; when the axes need different names, call each form with its own name.',
    parameters='**group** (`std::string`)\n    The name given to the groups of the x and y axes. An empty string leaves all of them.',
    returns='`Pane&`\n    The same pane, for chaining.',
    examples=[
        dict(id='readback', text='The same name on every covered axis. After the call, the group of each axis reads back as `group`; an axis the call does not cover is untouched.',
             code='auto fig = studio("align_xy_readback");\nauto& pane = fig.pane2("p");\npane.trend(std::vector<double>{0, 1, 2}, std::vector<double>{0, 1, 0});\npane.align_z("depth");\npane.align_xy("g");\nstd::cout << "x \'" << pane.x_align_group() << "\', y \'" << pane.y_align_group() << "\', z (not covered) \'" << pane.z_align_group() << "\'\\n";\nfig.save_svg("figure.svg");'),
        dict(id='grid', text='Small multiples. Four panes of a 2x2 mosaic with different data all call `align_xy("grid")`: the whole figure shares one x range and one y range, and the panes line up.',
             code='auto fig = studio("align_xy_grid");\nfig.mosaic(2, 2);\nconst double scales[] = {1.0, 4.0, 2.0, 8.0};\nfor (int i = 0; i < 4; ++i) {\n  auto& pane = fig.pane2("scale " + std::to_string(static_cast<int>(scales[i])));\n  pane.trend(std::vector<double>{0, 1, 2, 3}, std::vector<double>{0, scales[i], scales[i] / 2, scales[i]});\n  pane.align_xy("grid");\n}\nfig.save_svg("figure.svg");'),
        dict(id='captions', text="Captions follow the axes. One `x_caption` and one `y_caption` for the same group name each appear once for the whole figure; both match because the call set both axes' groups.",
             code='auto fig = studio("align_xy_captions");\nfig.mosaic(1, 2);\nfig.x_caption("grid", "time");\nfig.y_caption("grid", "level");\nfor (int i = 0; i < 2; ++i) {\n  auto& pane = fig.pane2("run " + std::to_string(i + 1));\n  pane.trend(std::vector<double>{0, 1, 2, 3}, std::vector<double>{0, 1.0 + i, 0.5, 2.0});\n  pane.align_xy("grid");\n}\nstd::cout << "x captions: " << fig.x_captions().size() << ", y captions: " << fig.y_captions().size() << "\\n";\nfig.save_svg("figure.svg");'),
        dict(id='override', text='Mixing with the single-axis calls. Calling `align_xy` and then `align_y` with another name changes only the y group; the x group keeps the shared name.',
             code='auto fig = studio("align_xy_override");\nauto& pane = fig.pane2("p");\npane.trend(std::vector<double>{0, 1, 2}, std::vector<double>{0, 1, 0});\npane.align_xy("g");\npane.align_y("other");\nstd::cout << "x \'" << pane.x_align_group() << "\', y \'" << pane.y_align_group() << "\'\\n";\nfig.save_svg("figure.svg");'),
    ],
    notes='- Equivalent to the single-axis calls with the same name; nothing else changes on the pane.\n- Not `noexcept`. Any string is accepted; the empty string leaves the groups.\n- On a planar pane a z group is stored but there is no z axis to share, so it has no visible effect.',
    see=['[`Pane::align_x`](align_x.md), [`align_y`](align_y.md), [`align_z`](align_z.md): one axis at a time, with the full account of what a group does.', '[`Pane::clear_align`](clear_align.md): leave all groups.', '[`Pane::x_align_group`](align_group_accessors.md): read a group back.'],
)
